<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Remove the secret and reconcile the operational estate (FR-C3)</title>
    <phase>3 Rollout</phase>
    <gate>032 soak complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>auth tag; the only irreversible step in the project.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Broad but mechanical sweep with an enumerated file list.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches .claude/constraints and .claude/patterns — main-session only; also irreversible.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>032</deps>
    <tags>auth,cleanup,scripts,documentation,skill-directives</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Remove BFF-API-ClientSecret from app settings and Key Vault including the lowercase alias, and reconcile the 11 PowerShell scripts and ~25 documents that reference it. This is the irreversible step; it happens only after the soak.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Be exhaustive — a missed path is a broken deploy.</role>
  <goal>No BFF-identity path resolves a secret, the Office add-in deploy still works, and no script or doc still instructs anyone to create one.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>One secret, five config keys, plus a SIXTH lowercase Key Vault alias bff-api-client-secret used by the Office add-in deploy — any removal that ignores it breaks the add-in. The inventory originally cited 2 scripts; an independent sweep found 11.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Configure-ProductionAppSettings.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Rotate-Secrets.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Reconcile-DemoEnvironment.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="032" status="pending">Soak complete on MI-FIC</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: remove from app settings FIRST, verify, THEN Key Vault. Not simultaneously.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: remove the secret from BOTH the production slot AND the staging slot. Task 001 mirrored all 213 app settings into the staging slot (deliberately, with reasoning -- notes/decisions/001-slot-creation.md Finding B), so 16 plaintext secret settings now exist in two places. Removing from one slot only leaves a live copy behind, and an app setting left on the staging slot will SWAP BACK INTO PRODUCTION on any future swap.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: on dev these are PLAINTEXT app-setting values, not Key Vault references -- so removal is app-setting deletion, not only Key Vault deletion. Confirmed live 2026-08-20: AzureAd__ClientSecret, API_CLIENT_SECRET, Dataverse__ClientSecret and AgentToken__ClientSecret all hold literal values. (This is NOT an auth.md violation: dev is explicitly carved out of the Key-Vault-references-only rule.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the lowercase alias bff-api-client-secret MUST be handled. Verify the Office add-in deploy path BEFORE removing it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: all 11 scripts must either stop referencing the secret or document why they still do. Enumerated in spec FR-C3.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: close exception E-3 — it is time-boxed to this project. Update the exception registry to reflect restored compliance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: .claude/ edits are main-session only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: do NOT remove per-customer SpeAdmin secrets (E-1) or PowerBi:ClientSecret (task 042 -- DEFERRED 2026-08-19, Power BI not yet adopted; this secret stays). Different credentials.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: SET Graph:Credentials:RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true IN THE SAME CHANGE that drops ClientSecret from the credential order. Booked by task 062 (implemented 2026-08-21). Rule 6 of IdentityConfigurationValidator fails startup outside Development when ClientSecret is still listed in the order, and it is OFF BY DEFAULT so that it could not block tasks 031/032 while the secret was still the intentional fallback. That default means the guard is silent until somebody turns it on -- if this task removes the secret but forgets the flag, the forcing function FR-F3 exists to provide simply never engages, and nothing will say so. Also update the credential census entry for OrderedCredentialClientProvider: its CredentialSource line must stop saying "transitional secret" (CredentialCensusTests maintenance procedure step 4).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Secret retirement, Key Vault, deployment scripts</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SECRET-ROTATION-PROCEDURES.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Verify the Office add-in deploy path's dependency on the lowercase alias.</step>
    <step>Remove the five config keys from dev app settings; verify the BFF still starts and OBO still works.</step>
    <step>Remove the Key Vault secret and the lowercase alias; re-verify the add-in deploy.</step>
    <step>Sweep the 11 scripts; remove or document each reference.</step>
    <step>Sweep the ~25 documents; correct every instruction that still tells a reader to create the secret.</step>
    <step>Close ADR-028 exception E-3; update .claude/constraints/auth.md and Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md:110,221.</step>
    <step>Clean up the orphaned Graph-API-ClientSecret alias (design §10 item 9).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any consumer of the secret is discovered that is NOT in the enumerated list — STOP and re-inventory before removing anything.</trigger>
    <trigger>The Office add-in deploy breaks — restore the alias immediately and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="modify">11 scripts + ~25 docs + .claude/ auth surfaces</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/033-secret-removal-record.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>The secret is removed from BOTH slots. Negative case: no secret-bearing app setting remains on the staging slot that could swap back into production later.</criterion>
    <criterion>No BFF-identity code path resolves a secret.</criterion>
    <criterion>The secret and the lowercase alias are gone from Key Vault.</criterion>
    <criterion>The Office add-in deploy still succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion>All 11 scripts either no longer reference the secret or document why they do.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADR-028 E-3 is closed and .claude/constraints/auth.md reflects the end state. Task 030
      carry-forward (ADR-check W-6) names two specifics that "end state" must include: (a) auth.md's header
      still reads `Last Updated: 2026-05-19` despite the A4 correction applied to lines 109-112 on 2026-08-17 —
      stale review metadata on THIS file is what let a false sentence survive three audits; (b) auth.md states
      the runtime rule but nothing about FIC PROVISIONING shape — add the same-tenant requirement and
      subject = principalId NOT clientId (the FR-B4 silent failure), now that task 030 built the repo's only
      automation for it.</criterion>
    <criterion>Task 030 carry-forward (ADR-check W-1): Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 in COMBINED mode
      (-CreateFederatedCredential without -FicOnly) still unconditionally mints a 24-month client secret and
      writes it to Key Vault — there is no -SkipClientSecret switch. Post-removal that would mint a
      per-customer secret on every customer-provisioning onboarding, which E-3 ("does not license expansion")
      reaches. Task 030 deliberately did NOT fix this: this task owns the file per FR-C3, and the secret was
      still the live rollback mechanism at the time. Resolve it here.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: SpeAdmin per-customer secrets (E-1) and PowerBi:ClientSecret are untouched.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: the full §6.1 OBO checklist still passes after removal.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
